/**
 * Module 3: Research & Validation (Scientific Laboratory & Benchmarking Hub)
 *
 * Operational Responsibilities:
 * 1. Centralized scientific research presentation, keeping research analysis
 *    strictly separated from live operational views (Detection and Early Warning).
 * 2. Clear scientific provenance taxonomy:
 *    - Published paper results
 *    - Results reproduced from supplied datasets
 *    - Results generated by local experiments
 *    - Synthetic or digital-twin simulation results
 *    - Results obtained from actual physical hardware
 *    - Results not yet validated
 * 3. Interactive sub-tabs for:
 *    - Framework & Hypotheses (H1–H4)
 *    - Baseline Models & Ablation Studies (SVM, RF, CNN vs Proposed)
 *    - Adversarial Evaluation (AER / FHER under AIS/sensor noise)
 *    - Robustness & Uncertainty Calibration (ECE, Reliability Diagrams)
 *    - Real Submarine DAS Field Deployments
 *    - In-Browser Cryptographic Provenance Verifier (SHA-256)
 *
 * Scientific & Safety Integrity:
 * - Historical benchmarks are NEVER shown as live detection results.
 * - Simulated results are NEVER presented as physical hardware measurements.
 * - Research configurations do not silently alter live operational thresholds.
 */

